    "title": "Concession Clauses",
    "title_ko": "양보절",
    "focus_axis": "grammar"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "Concession clauses acknowledge a contrasting fact before making a main point: 'Even though it was expensive, we bought it.' 'Even if it rains, we'll go.' (hypothetical) 'While I understand your point, I disagree.' (contrast, more formal).",
    "explanation_ko": "양보절은 주된 요점을 말하기 전에 대조되는 사실을 인정합니다: 'Even though it was expensive, we bought it.' 'Even if it rains, we'll go.'(가정) 'While I understand your point, I disagree.'(대조, 더 격식적).",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "Even though I was tired, I kept working.",
        "ko": "피곤했지만 저는 계속 일했어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "Even if it's difficult, I'll try.",
        "ko": "어렵더라도 저는 시도할 거예요."
      },
      {
        "en": "While I respect your opinion, I see it differently.",
        "ko": "당신의 의견을 존중하지만 저는 다르게 봐요."
      }
    ]
  },
